WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
A container ship carries goods
from one continent to another.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.170
Money flows through
open financial markets.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.950
People meet fences, visas
and passport queues.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.030
In 2024, there were 304
million international migrants:

5
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.890
just 3.7 per cent of people.

6
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.450
Goods and money cross borders with ease.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.090
So why is it so much harder for people?

8
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.590
In this mission, you'll compare
moving within one country,

9
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.250
within a bloc of countries,
and across the whole world.

10
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.530
Then you'll see how migration
changes a country's population,

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.670
and why the same flows are seen so
differently on each side of a border.

12
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain why people find it
so much harder than goods and money to

13
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.790
cross borders.
